<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.080 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.080 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE SEPT 30, 1998</p>
<p>			     $18.255 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.080    Awarded At	99.851	6.000</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.060    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.011    17 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.64 Times</p>
<p>    U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)	    MATURITY 30.Sep.98</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 30.Sep.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 25.Sep.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  18.255 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912827Z47</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   48.171			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.452				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.000</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   2.250			   PRICE	 99.851</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.011-6.080 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.080</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.17 PCT AT AUCTION ON 27.AUG.96</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.053 PCT AT AUCTION 29.MAY.96</p>
